WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.806
Vinnie looked so worried that Helene ran over to him.

2
00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:09.158
"What’s wrong?" she said.

3
00:00:09.159 --> 00:00:11.094
Vinnie explained.

4
00:00:11.095 --> 00:00:15.811
"I have to keep the soup away from the king," he cried.

5
00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:18.874
"I’ll help," said Helene.

6
00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:23.129
They followed the servant carrying the tray of soup.

7
00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:27.894
In the palace, Mandy was still searching for Helene.

8
00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:31.005
She walked down another hallway.

9
00:00:31.006 --> 00:00:34.342
She heard noises.

10
00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:37.880
Quietly she opened the nearest door.

11
00:00:37.881 --> 00:00:41.088
The room was full of billiard tables.

12
00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:44.494
Men, including King Louis, were playing.

13
00:00:44.495 --> 00:00:48.410
"Oh, Your Majesty," one man laughed.

14
00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:50.159
"You win again!

15
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.271
You are truly the champion of this game."

16
00:00:53.272 --> 00:00:55.468
King Louis smiled.

17
00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:58.677
Then he walked into the next room.

18
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:02.275
Mandy followed, keeping out of sight.

19
00:01:02.276 --> 00:01:05.751
It was a dining room with a long table.

20
00:01:05.752 --> 00:01:09.000
Waiting servants held trays of food.

21
00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:11.044
"Bring me my soup!"

22
00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:13.806
said the king as he sat down.

23
00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:18.281
Mandy saw her brother and Helene right behind the servants.

24
00:01:18.282 --> 00:01:20.410
They looked scared.

25
00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:24.011
Mandy waved, but they didn’t see her.

26
00:01:24.012 --> 00:01:31.886
"Ah, my favorite soup!" the king said.

27
00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:35.200
At that moment, Vinnie jumped out.

28
00:01:35.201 --> 00:01:38.080
"Don’t eat that!" he yelled.

29
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:43.158
Startled, the servant dropped the soup into the king’s lap.

30
00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.150
"You idiot!"

31
00:01:45.151 --> 00:01:47.940
King Louis leaped from his seat.

32
00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:52.147
"Your Majesty, are you all right?" cried the servant.

33
00:01:52.148 --> 00:01:54.476
Everyone ran to the king.

34
00:01:54.477 --> 00:01:57.807
They tried to wipe off the spilled soup.

35
00:01:57.808 --> 00:02:02.480
"Vinnie! Helene!" Mandy shouted loudly.

36
00:02:02.481 --> 00:02:04.626
They ran to her.

37
00:02:04.627 --> 00:02:08.271
"We’d better get away!" Helene cried.

38
00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:12.606
"Oh, look at the royal clothing," said someone.

39
00:02:12.607 --> 00:02:16.357
"His coat is ruined," said another.

40
00:02:16.358 --> 00:02:20.342
"And his best hat," a servant whispered.

41
00:02:20.343 --> 00:02:22.275
"What a mess!"

42
00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:24.937
The king looked up and screamed:

43
00:02:24.938 --> 00:02:27.402
"That boy! Stop him!"

44
00:02:27.403 --> 00:02:29.763
Everyone looked around.

45
00:02:29.764 --> 00:02:33.448
In the confusion, the children had escaped.

46
00:02:33.449 --> 00:02:36.823
The children ran down a long hallway.

47
00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:39.922
"Over here!" cried Helene.

48
00:02:39.923 --> 00:02:43.403
They stopped to catch their breath in a corner.

49
00:02:43.404 --> 00:02:46.066
The guards were far behind.

50
00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.614
Vinnie pulled out the photo.

51
00:02:48.615 --> 00:02:53.335
"We have to get to a fountain with golden frogs," he said.

52
00:02:53.336 --> 00:02:57.735
"You must mean the Fountain of Latona," said Helene.

53
00:02:57.736 --> 00:02:59.845
"It has many frogs on it.

54
00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:03.029
It’s behind the palace. I’ll show you."

55
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.151
The children followed her.

56
00:03:07.152 --> 00:03:09.734
Along the way Mandy asked:

57
00:03:09.735 --> 00:03:12.238
"Why did you stop King Louis?"

58
00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:14.359
Vinnie explained.

59
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.870
"Would the king really kill someone because of his soup?" asked Mandy.

60
00:03:19.871 --> 00:03:24.734
"Only if it was truly poisoned!" laughed Helene.

61
00:03:24.735 --> 00:03:30.894
"Look, Mandy! The frogs in the picture are glowing blue!" Vinnie shouted.

62
00:03:30.895 --> 00:03:33.672
"What?" asked Helene.

63
00:03:33.673 --> 00:03:37.868
"Nothing," said Mandy.

64
00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:39.405
"There it is!"

65
00:03:39.406 --> 00:03:42.879
Helene pointed ahead.

66
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.475
"The fountain was inspired by an ancient Greek goddess.

67
00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:50.090
She turned people into frogs if they insulted her."

68
00:03:50.091 --> 00:03:54.674
"Wow, sounds cruel," gulped Vinnie.

69
00:03:54.675 --> 00:03:56.473
Helene giggled.

70
00:03:56.474 --> 00:04:02.108
"Some people think King Louis built it to send his people a message:

71
00:04:02.109 --> 00:04:04.470
obey your king!

72
00:04:04.471 --> 00:04:06.740
Anyway, I have to get back to work.

73
00:04:06.741 --> 00:04:08.181
See you later?"

74
00:04:08.182 --> 00:04:10.752
Mandy gave her a hug.

75
00:04:10.753 --> 00:04:15.613
"Well . . . good-bye," she said, then paused.

76
00:04:15.614 --> 00:04:18.199
"I am so glad I met you!"

77
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.961
Helene looked confused.

78
00:04:20.962 --> 00:04:25.621
When Vinnie and Mandy got to the fountain, they looked back.

79
00:04:25.622 --> 00:04:29.598
Helene was walking up the steps waving.

80
00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:35.041
The grand Palace of Versailles was as beautiful as ever.

81
00:04:35.042 --> 00:04:38.434
"The frogs are glowing red," said Vinnie.

82
00:04:38.435 --> 00:04:46.863
"We’re going home."

